; GraphEdit whose ZOOM-OUT button is disabled, the only state either zoom
; button can take that a scene file reaches. `set_zoom_custom` clamps `zoom`
; against the bounds as they stand (graph_edit.cpp:2434) and only then presses
; `zoom_minus_button->set_disabled(zoom == zoom_min)` (:2445) — and it returns
; BEFORE that line whenever the clamp changed nothing (:2435-2437). So no file
; can disable a button by parking `zoom` on a bound directly: the value has to
; MOVE onto it. `zoom = 0.5` lands inside the constructor's own range (:3175
; -3177), then `zoom_min = 1.0` re-runs `set_zoom(zoom)` (:2487) and drags it
; back up to 1.0, which equals the new min.
; The stored `zoom` therefore ends at its own default, so this scene draws the
; family's picture at scale 1 with ONE pixel difference: the zoom-out icon at
; `icon_disabled_color`'s alpha of 0.4 (default_theme.cpp:169) instead of 1.
; A previewer that read `zoom` as authored would draw the whole graph at 0.5,
; and one that ignored the order would leave the icon opaque. No other fixture
; writes a zoom bound at all, and the only one that writes `zoom` sits it well
; inside both bounds, where neither effect exists.

; Every fixture in this family shares one GraphEdit rect and one GraphNode,
; and `scroll_offset` is deliberately ABSENT from all but
; unit-graph-edit-scroll-offset-clamped.tscn, which exists to move it:
; GraphEdit's own `set_scroll_offset` clamps against min/max bounds no laid-out
; child has widened while a scene's properties are applied (graph_edit.cpp:407),
; so an authored offset moves the grid, the nodes AND the minimap camera at once
; and would mask the one variable each file exists to move.
